      "ruled": "2026-08-01",
      "why": "HELD OUT by user ruling 2026-08-01 (Issue #261 wave-2 packet, item 2b). The ruling is REJECT -- the agent should play Harlequin -- and it is NOT satisfiable by the refresh SHED, which is why it moves to T3/T4 rather than staying open against a swap that cannot answer it.\n\nMEASURED, so the owner does not re-derive it. This frame and ep83037962 f49 are the same board to the shed: opponent hand 7 on both, so STRIP is +12 on both, so both decline iff shed > 32. The user ruled them OPPOSITE ways (play here, refuse there). Two fixes were built and reverted, and NEITHER can hold both:\n  succession spike value 30 -> 15 : f34 shed 33.0 -> 16.5 PLAYS (ok), f49 PLAYS (breaks it)\n  succession re-access 0 -> 0.77  : f34 shed 33.0 -> 16.5 PLAYS (ok), f49 46.1 -> 24.1 PLAYS (breaks it)\nThe two Basic {W} do not carry f49: they price 2.49 each, correctly -- 8 Energy outs in a 43-card pool over 5 draws is a 66% recovery, so the fund-attack slot discounts to 31% of tier.\n\nTHE AXIS IS CERTAINTY, NOT MAGNITUDE. The shed is a RISK-NEUTRAL expectation: it prices a 79%-recoverable Mega Starmie ex at 79% recovered. The user's f49 reasoning is a RISK calculation -- 'in our hand is what we need to respond to the possible KO with a new Starmie with energy, THAT GUARANTEE is what we risk' -- and the odds bear it out: ~40% to redraw both pieces against ~15pp of KO reduction (their Ignition -> Nebula Beam 210 is exact lethal on a 210 HP Active; 3 unseen in a pool of 45 gives 45.2% at hand 8 vs 30.4% at hand 5). The old resupply=0.0 closing edge was a crude proxy for that preference; it over-fires here, where the same card has 8 outs at 67% and the rest of the hand is dead (Salvatore wastes -- the last Mega Starmie is PRIZED with none in deck -- and neither benched Staryu can be evolved this turn, rules.md 4).\n\nExpressing 'guaranteed vs expected under an imminent KO' is variance, which lives in the gamble machinery (ADR-0039) and T3's state_value, not in a slot's resupply term. Returns to gating when that exists -- delete this owner then.\n\nNOTE for the owner: a doom-read theory was tested and REFUTED. active_doomed reads True here and it is NOT a worst-case artifact -- the opponent is Kyogre / Mega Abomasnow ex (Read confident; 2x Kyogre benched), Hammer-lanche {W}{W} is payable NOW with 2 attached, and the rep build puts 29 Basic {W} in 44 unseen (66%), so its EXPECTED roll is ~300-395 against a 330 HP Active. Both frames are genuinely doomed; doom does not separate them.\n\nOWNER: #262 (POC-T3, state_value) -- it owns the prize-denominated scalar the variance term must live in, alongside the gamble machinery (ADR-0039)."
